.TH "pa-notify" "1" "19 November 2026" "pa-notify(1)" "User manual"

.SH NAME

pa-notify \(em PulseAudio or PipeWire volume notification

.SH SYNOPSIS

.PP
\fBpa-notify\fR [\fBOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION

.PP
\fBpa-notify\fR is a PulseAudio or PipeWire volume notification utility. It gets information from the sound server using libpulse and shows notifications using libnotify. If the connection to the sound server is lost (for example, when the PipeWire or PulseAudio daemon is restarted), \fBpa-notify\fR automatically reconnects. If showing a notification fails (for example, right after the notification daemon has been restarted), the notification is retried on the next volume change.

.SH OPTIONS

.IP "\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR" 5
Show help options
.IP "\fB-d\fR, \fB--debug\fR" 5
Enable debug information
.IP "\fB-t\fR, \fB--timeout\fR" 5
Notification timeout in seconds (-1 - default notification timeout, 0 - notification never expires)
.IP "\fB-u\fR, \fB--urgency\fR" 5
Notification urgency (0 - low, 1 - normal, 2 - critical)

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
\fBpa-notify\fR
Run with default settings.
.TP
\fBpa-notify \-t 2 \-u 1\fR
Show each notification for two seconds with normal urgency.
